Independent implementation (Python stdlib decimal, no shared code, no mpmath): assembled the periodized Bargmann–Fock covariance Gram (L=24, weights ρ_{m,n}=exp(−|ξ|²/2), ξ=2π(m,n)/24) of the six pins {f,f_x,f_y at ±(1/40,0)} plus the nine midpoint jets, at r=1/20. The sum factorizes over the two frequency axes (all points on y=0), evaluated at dps=55 with Fourier cutoff |m|,|n|≤100 (truncation error ~e^{−342}≈10^{−149}, negligible). Positive-definiteness certified by exact-arithmetic Cholesky (a symmetric matrix is PD iff Cholesky completes with positive pivots); λ_min by inverse-power iteration on the Cholesky factor.

RESULTS (variance-normalized / correlation matrix):
